<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Ultrainfo (converted from the organizer's official GPX download)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata>
    <name>Badger Mountain Challenge 100 course</name>
    <desc>The full 100-mile course — two trips on the 50-mile out-and-back from Badger Mountain Trailhead Park in Richland, WA to the Chandler Butte turnaround. Points and elevations copy the organizer's official GPX download ("THE BMC 100MILER", linked from the 100-miler page; retrieved 2026-08-13), converted from its route points to track points. The line GPS-measures 99.00 miles with a 106-foot closure against the aid chart's 100-mile frame, which governs pass miles. Station waypoints sit on the line at each station's first chart mile; the directional-only McBee Ridge markers get outbound and inbound waypoints because the chart's two ridge rows sit about 0.9 mile apart on the line.</desc>
    <link href="http://www.badgermountainchallenge.com/p/100-miler.html"><text>BMC 100-miler page</text></link>
  </metadata>
